### Please describe the problem in your own words.

While setting up an old MacBook Pro (2012) to run as a git-annex disk repository, I found that the [current macOS Standalone build](https://downloads.kitenet.net/git-annex/OSX/current/10.15_Catalina/) no longer runs on macOS 10.15 / Catalina, despite the directory name.

It looks like some of the dependencies used are only built for macOS 14 or later (which is unsurprising, as I believe current macOS Developer tools force macOS 14 or later).  And macOS 10.15 went entirely unsupported earlier this year (not even extended security support), so it's unsurprising it's no longer a build target.  (IIRC macOS 14 is also the oldest version that HomeBrew builds against now.)

I'm reporting it just as a suggestion that maybe the macOS build directory for downloads gets renamed to, eg, macOS 14, which is [macOS Sonomoa](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MacOS_Sonoma), to reflect the current situation.  And the [OSX](https://git-annex.branchable.com/install/OSX/) page gets updated to reflect that, and maybe link to some older build for "old macOS".

(macOS 10.15 is the last macOS version to run on this MacBook Pro 2012, so I'll try digging back into older builds for a git-annex build that will run on macOS 10.15.  Fortunately it's very internal, so latest-security-patches isn't a huge concern.  This is just hardware upcycling while it still works.)

### What steps will reproduce the problem?

On a macOS 10.15.8 (Catalina) system, install the [current macOS Standalone build](https://downloads.kitenet.net/git-annex/OSX/current/10.15_Catalina/), add it to `$PATH`, and then run `git annex version`.  Observe it fails with a missing symbol:

```
dyld: Symbol not found: __ZNSt3__113basic_filebufIcNS_11char_traitsIcEEE4openEPKcj
```

apparently from a dependency `.dylib`, which AFAICT is `libbotan-3.13`, and it looks like that dylib dependency was built for macOS 14.

### What version of git-annex are you using? On what operating system?

macOS standalone build in the 10.15_Catalina directory today, dated `2026-10-26 14:37`.  I'd assumed it was 10.20261026, but I think it might be 10.20261021 based on the App embedded metadata.

### Please provide any additional information below.

```
ewen@dagoba:~$ uname -a
Darwin dagoba 19.6.0 Darwin Kernel Version 19.6.0: Tue Jun 21 21:18:39 PDT 2022; root:xnu-6153.141.66~1/RELEASE_X86_64 x86_64
ewen@dagoba:~$ git annex version
dyld: Symbol not found: __ZNSt3__113basic_filebufIcNS_11char_traitsIcEEE4openEPKcj
  Referenced from: /Applications/OpenSource/git-annex.app/Contents/MacOS/bundle/D (which was built for Mac OS X 14.0)
  Expected in: /usr/lib/libc++.1.dylib

error: git-annex died of signal 6
ewen@dagoba:~$ 
ewen@dagoba:~$ ls -l /Applications/OpenSource/git-annex.app/Contents/MacOS/bundle/D
lrwxr-xr-x  1 ewen  admin  43 Oct 26 11:16 /Applications/OpenSource/git-annex.app/Contents/MacOS/bundle/D -> usr/local/opt/botan/lib/libbotan-3.13.dylib
ewen@dagoba:~$ 
```

### Have you had any luck using git-annex before? (Sometimes we get tired of reading bug reports all day and a lil' positive end note does wonders)

Yes, git-annex has been very useful for years!

(Also, related to [my previous bug report about more recent macOS Intel, dying with Signal 4](https://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/10.20261006__58___addurl__58___git-annex_died_of_signal_4/) I can report that HomeBrew have updated their build options to no longer pin a pre-release package, and seems to be back to building against an older `crypton` without the problem.  So that's encouraging!)

> Renamed the build. [[done]] --[[Joey]]
